# Innocent Blood and a token: a creature token is a creature, so Bot1 may sacrifice one of the three Rabbits Hop to It made
# (the second, not the first). It goes to the graveyard for an instant and then ceases to exist (CR 111.7, 704.5d), so no
# graveyard holds it: Bot1's graveyard is just Hop to It and Innocent Blood, and two Rabbits stay. Bot2 has no creature.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Hop to It
Swamp
Innocent Blood
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hop to It.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Innocent Blood.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rabbit Token#2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Pearl; Plains; Rabbit Token; Rabbit Token; Swamp
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Graveyard = Innocent Blood; Hop to It
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
